.PP
For a shorter quick-reference page see
.BR nmaprs (1).
.SH NAME
nmaprs, nms \- high-performance parallel network scanner with
nmap-compatible CLI surface (Rust)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nmaprs
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ TARGETS ]
.br
.B nms
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ TARGETS ]
.PP
.B nms
is the shorter form of
.BR nmaprs
\(em same binary, quicker to type.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nmaprs
is a Rust-native network scanner that speaks
.BR nmap (1)'s
CLI dialect
.RB ( "nmap \-\-help"
plus the long-option set from upstream
.BR nmap.cc ,
e.g.
.BR \-\-resolve-all ,
.BR \-\-defeat-rst-ratelimit ,
.BR \-\-versiondb ,
.BR \-oM / \-oH ,
.BR \-\-vv ,
.B \-\-proxy
as an alias of
.BR \-\-proxies ).
.PP
.B Wired at the packet level
for raw TCP scans: evasion flags
.RB ( \-g
source port,
.BR \-\-badsum ,
.B \-D
decoys,
.B \-S
source spoofing,
.BR \-\-data / \-\-data-string / \-\-data-length ).
.BR \-\-ttl ,
.BR \-f / \-\-mtu
fragmentation and
.B \-\-ip-options
are parsed and validated for CLI parity but are not applied to the
emitted packets.
.PP
.B \-\-proxies
routes TCP-connect scans through SOCKS4 or HTTP CONNECT proxies.
.B \-\-dns-servers
resolves targets via custom DNS servers via
.BR hickory-resolver .
.B \-\-spoof-mac
spoofs the source MAC on ARP discovery frames.
.B \-\-stats-every
prints periodic scan progress with ETC and probes/sec.
.PP
Multiple
.B \-iL
lines and CLI targets resolve
.B in parallel
(order preserved) with the same
.BR \-\-max-parallelism / \-\-min-parallelism / "timing template"
cap as port probes.
.PP
.B nmaprs is not a byte-for-byte reimplementation of nmap.
The full NSE Lua runtime is
.B not
embedded; OS detection is partial
.RB ( IPv4
raw probes + MatchPoints scoring against
.BR nmap-os-db ;
.B IPv6
TTL heuristic only). For authoritative behavior use
.BR nmap (1).
.SH "1.  INVOCATION"
With no flags,
.B nmaprs
performs a TCP-connect scan
.RB ( \-sT )
of nmap's default top-1000 TCP ports against the given
.IR TARGETS .
.PP
.B Privilege auto-detection:
on startup
.B nmaprs
calls
.BR geteuid (2);
when not root it downgrades from raw SYN
.RB ( \-sS )
to TCP connect
.RB ( \-sT )
and rejects raw-only modes
.RB ( \-sO ,
.BR \-sI ,
SCTP). Use
.B \-\-privileged
to force raw mode (kernel may still reject without
.BR CAP_NET_RAW )
or
.B \-\-unprivileged
to force connect mode even as root.
.PP
.B Target syntax (same as nmap):
.PP
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
.B Form|.B Example
hostname|\fBscanme.nmap.org\fR
IPv4|\fB192.168.1.1\fR
IPv6|\fB2001:db8::1\fR (requires \fB-6\fR)
CIDR v4|\fB10.0.0.0/24\fR
CIDR v6|\fB2001:db8::/64\fR
range|\fB10.0.0.1-100\fR or \fB10.0.0-255.1\fR
.TE
.SH "2.  TARGET SELECTION"
.TP
.B \-\-iL \fIFILE\fR
Read targets, one per line, from
.IR FILE .
Multiple
.B \-iL
flags merge in parallel (order preserved).
.TP
.B \-\-iR \fINUM\fR
Pick
.I NUM
random hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude \fITARGETS\fR
Comma-separated hosts/networks to skip.
.TP
.B \-\-excludefile \fIFILE\fR
File with hosts/networks to skip (one per line).
.TP
.B \-\-resolve-all
By default DNS returns one address (nmap's "first only"). Pass this
to scan every resolved address per name.
.SH "3.  HOST DISCOVERY"
.TP
.B \-sL
List-scan only \(em do not send probes.
.TP
.B \-sn
Ping scan: skip the port scan. Per-host raw ICMP echo via
.B pnet
(privileged), falls back to system
.BR ping (8)
/
.BR ping6 (8).
Output paths
.RB ( \-oN ,
.BR \-oG ,
.BR \-oX ,
.BR \-oS )
write host-up lines like the port-scan path.
.TP
.BR \-Pn ", " \-\-no-ping
Treat all hosts as online; skip discovery entirely.
.TP
.BI \-PS [ PORTLIST ]
TCP SYN discovery on the given ports (default 80, 443).
.TP
.BI \-PA [ PORTLIST ]
TCP ACK discovery (RST/SYN-ACK indicates up).
.TP
.BI \-PU [ PORTLIST ]
UDP discovery probe (default port 40125).
.TP
.BI \-PY [ PORTLIST ]
SCTP INIT discovery (default port 80). Same raw SCTP engines as
.BR \-sY .
.TP
.BI \-PO [ PROTOS ]
IP-protocol ping (default 1,2,4). Same engines as
.BR \-sO .
Host is up if any probe is open or closed.
.TP
.B \-PE
ICMP echo.
.TP
.B \-PP
ICMP timestamp request (IPv4, Unix raw ICMP).
.TP
.B \-PM
ICMP address-mask request (IPv4, Unix raw ICMP).
.TP
ARP ping (no flag)
Auto-runs for local-subnet IPv4 hosts; disable with
.BR \-\-disable-arp-ping .
nmap's
.B \-PR
is not accepted.
.TP
.B \-n
Never resolve DNS.
.TP
.B \-R
Always resolve DNS (default: only for live hosts).
.TP
.B \-\-dns-servers \fISERVERS\fR
Comma-separated IPs of custom DNS resolvers (uses
.BR hickory-resolver
instead of the system stub).
.TP
.B \-\-system-dns
Force the system resolver.
.TP
.B \-\-traceroute
Trace hop path to each host using the system
.BR traceroute (8)
/
.BR tracert
binary. Up to
.B min(parallelism, 32)
hosts run concurrently; output stays in target order.
.SH "4.  SCAN TECHNIQUES"
.SS TCP connect (\-sT)
Default when unprivileged. Async, parallel, timeout-bound.
.SS TCP SYN (\-sS)
Default when privileged. Raw IPv4 + IPv6 TCP via
.BR pnet :
RST \(-> closed, SYN/ACK \(-> open. Pipelined per family with dedicated
recv thread + main-thread sends; sharded across up to 16 concurrent
pipelines per family (bounded by
.BR effective_probe_concurrency() ).
Mixed v4+v6 targets run both families concurrently via
.BR tokio::join .
Falls back to TCP connect per address family on raw failure.
.SS TCP NULL / FIN / Xmas / Maimon (\-sN / \-sF / \-sX / \-sM)
Same raw sharded pipeline as
.BR \-sS .
Maimon sends FIN+ACK.
.SS TCP ACK (\-sA)
Firewall mapping. RST \(-> unfiltered, no reply \(-> filtered. No TCP
connect fallback on raw failure (connect can't produce ACK-scan
states).
.SS TCP Window (\-sW)
Same ACK probes; RST with non-zero TCP window \(-> open, RST with zero
window \(-> closed (BSD-derived stacks); no reply \(-> filtered.
.SS UDP (\-sU)
Reply \(-> open. Raw ICMP listener (privileged) classifies destination
unreachable codes: port-unreachable \(-> closed; other unreachable
(IPv4 type 3 / ICMPv6 type 1) \(-> filtered. Unix uses one
.BR poll (2)
+ burst-recv thread when both IPv4 and IPv6 targets are in play.
.B closed wins over filtered.
With
.BR \-\-min-hostgroup / \-\-max-hostgroup ,
ICMP listener threads start once per scan (not per batch).
.SS SCTP INIT / COOKIE_ECHO (\-sY / \-sZ)
CRC32c SCTP segments. IPv4 Layer-3 full datagrams; IPv6 raw SCTP
(protocol 132) like IPv6 TCP. Pipelined recv + up to 16 shards per
family. Mixed v4+v6 runs both engines concurrently
.RB ( tokio::join ).
INIT-ACK / COOKIE-ACK \(-> open, ABORT \(-> closed.
.B Privileged
raw socket.
.SS Idle scan (\-sI \fIZOMBIE\fR[:\fIPROBEPORT\fR])
Spoofed TCP SYN (source = zombie) toward targets; sequential IP-ID
sampling on the zombie (RST to a closed probe port, default 65535) so
global IP-ID deltas stay interpretable. Delta \(>= 2 \(-> open, else
closed; probe / RST failures \(-> filtered. IPv4 only;
.B privileged
raw send.
.SS FTP bounce (\-b \fIuser:pass@host:port\fR)
Parallel
.B buffer_unordered
sessions (one control connection per probe). IPv4 only
.RB ( PORT ).
Maps 150/125/250 vs 425/426/421 to open/closed; misconfigured/strict
servers may return filtered.
.SS IP protocol (\-sO)
IPv4: raw IPv4 headers; ICMPv4 protocol-unreachable (type 3 code 2)
\(-> closed. IPv6 (Unix): raw IPv6
.RB ( IPPROTO_RAW
+
.BR IPV6_HDRINCL )
with Next Header = probe; ICMPv6 Parameter Problem type 4 code 1
\(-> closed. Mixed v4+v6 runs both engines concurrently. Sharded recv
+ up to 16 pipelines per family.
.BI \-p
takes protocol numbers
.BR 0..=255 ;
omit
.B \-p
to probe all 256.
.B \-F
limits protocols to
.BR nmap-protocols
(embedded as
.BR data/nmap_ip_protocols_fast.txt ),
matching nmap's
.B "[P:0-]"
fast selection.
.SS Combined scans (\-sS \-sU, etc.)
Multiple scan types run sequentially in one pass (e.g. SYN + UDP).
.SS \-\-scanflags \fIFLAGS\fR
Custom TCP flag set for raw TCP scans. Names:
.B SYN, ACK, FIN, RST, PSH, URG, ECE, CWR.
Separators: space, comma, pipe, or glued (e.g.
.BR SYNACK ).
Sequence/ack numbers follow nmap-style rules for SYN vs ACK probes;
recv classification still follows the selected scan type. Ignored
(warning) when scan type isn't raw TCP.
.SH "5.  PORT SPECIFICATION"
.TP
.BI \-p " PORTS"
Port ranges
.RB ( 1-65535 ,
.BR 22,80,443 ,
.B U:53,T:22
).
.B \-p \-
shorthand for all 65536.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude-ports \fIPORTS\fR
Skip these ports (ignored when
.B \-\-allports
is set).
.TP
.B \-F
Fast: nmap's top-100 frequency list.
.TP
.B \-r
Scan sequentially (don't randomize).
.TP
.B \-\-top-ports \fIN\fR
Scan the
.I N
highest-ratio ports.
.TP
.B \-\-port-ratio \fIRATIO\fR
Scan ports whose nmap frequency is at least
.IR RATIO .
.SH "6.  SERVICE / VERSION / SCRIPT"
.TP
.BR \-sV ", " \-\-version-scan
Load
.B nmap-service-probes:
TCP + UDP
.B Probe
blocks, with
.B ports / sslports
(TLS via
.B rustls
when port matches
.BR sslports ),
.B rarity
vs
.BR \-\-version-intensity ,
and
.B match / softmatch
with full template fields:
.BR "p/" " product, " "v/" " version, " "i/" " info, " "o/" " OS, " "d/" " device, " "cpe:/" " CPE."
Perl-only regex features omitted. Parallel per open port.
.TP
.B \-\-version-intensity \fI0-9\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-version-light
.RI ( =2 )
.TQ
.B \-\-version-all
.RI ( =9 )
.TQ
.B \-\-version-trace
Increase or trace version-scan effort.
.TP
.B \-sC
Default built-in scripts
.RB ( default
+
.BR banner ;
Lua NSE
.B not
embedded).
.TP
.B \-\-script \fIEXPR\fR
Run specified built-in scripts (no Lua NSE).
.TP
.B \-\-script-args \fIARGS\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-script-args-file \fIFILE\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-script-trace
.TQ
.B \-\-script-updatedb
.TQ
.B \-\-script-help \fIEXPR\fR
Compat shims for nmap parity (no Lua engine).
.SH "7.  OS DETECTION"
.TP
.B \-O
.B IPv4
(privileged): raw Layer-3 probes + nmap-os-db MatchPoints scoring
when
.B \-\-datadir
has the DB and the scan found both open and closed TCP ports (and
.B not
.B \-\-osscan-limit
with no open TCP). Falls back to ICMP TTL +
.B Class
titles from the legacy DB parse.
.B IPv6:
TTL-style guess only (no raw OS probe engine yet).
.TP
.B \-\-osscan-limit
Skip OS pass when no open TCP ports.
.TP
.B \-\-osscan-guess
.RI ( \-\-fuzzy )
Limit examples / show probable matches.
.TP
.B \-\-max-os-tries \fIN\fR
Maximum OS detect tries.
.SH "8.  TIMING & PERFORMANCE"
.TP
.B \-\-timing \fI0-5\fR
.TQ
.B \-T \fI0-5\fR
Timing template:
.B T0
paranoid,
.B T1
sneaky,
.B T2
polite,
.B T3
normal,
.B T4
aggressive,
.B T5
insane.
.TP
.B \-\-min-rate \fIN\fR
Send at least
.I N
probes/second. Must be \(<=
.B \-\-max-rate
when both set. Without
.BR \-\-max-parallelism ,
parallelism is raised toward
.B min(min-rate, 65535)
when that exceeds the timing template.
.TP
.B \-\-max-rate \fIN\fR
Global cap on probe
.B starts
per second (TCP connect, UDP, raw half-open TCP, SCTP, IP protocol;
mixed IPv4+IPv6 share one limiter).
.TP
.B \-\-min-parallelism \fIN\fR
.TQ
.BR \-M ", " \-\-max-parallelism " " \fIN\fR
Concurrent probe count bounds.
.TP
.B \-\-min-hostgroup \fIN\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-max-hostgroup \fIN\fR
Split resolved host list into batches before building port work.
Omit both: scan all hosts in one batch. Set only one: the other
defaults to 1 or 1024 (nmap-style). When both differ: uniform random
in
.RB [ min , max ]
(last batch may be smaller).
.B \-\-resume
filters per batch and merges at end.
.TP
.B \-\-host-timeout \fITIME\fR
Per-host wall clock from first probe. Remaining ports become
.B filtered
with reason
.B host-timeout
(TCP connect, UDP, raw half-open TCP, IP protocol; mixed v4+v6 share
one per-
.B IpAddr
clock).
.TP
.B \-\-max-retries \fIN\fR
Extra attempts after probe timeout. Total tries =
.BR "1 + N" .
Applies to TCP connect, UDP, raw half-open TCP, IP protocol, FTP
bounce, SCTP, idle scan. Retry rounds omit scan-delay and rate pacer.
.TP
.B \-\-min-rtt-timeout \fITIME\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-max-rtt-timeout \fITIME\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-initial-rtt-timeout \fITIME\fR
RTT bounds for adaptive probe timeout.
.B "max \(>= min"
required when both set.
.TP
.B \-\-scan-delay \fITIME\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-max-scan-delay \fITIME\fR
Per-probe delay before send/connect: fixed
.BR scan-delay ,
or uniform random in
.RB [ scan-delay , max-scan-delay ]
when both set.
.B "max \(>= min"
required.
.TP
.B \-\-defeat-rst-ratelimit
Reduce wait for RST replies from rate-limited hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-defeat-icmp-ratelimit
Reduce wait for ICMP replies from rate-limited hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-nsock-engine \fIENGINE\fR
Accepted and ignored; reserved for nmap parity.
.TP
.B \-\-stats-every \fITIME\fR
Periodic scan progress to stderr (% done, ETC, probes/sec).
Per-probe granularity for TCP connect.
.SH "9.  FIREWALL / IDS EVASION"
Unless a flag says otherwise below, the evasion flags in this section are wired
.B at the packet level
for raw TCP scans.
.TP
.B \-g \fIPORT\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-source-port \fIPORT\fR
Spoof source port (default fast SYN scans use random high port).
.TP
.B \-\-ttl \fIVAL\fR
Set IP TTL. Parsed and validated only; not yet applied to emitted packets.
.TP
.B \-\-badsum
Use a bad TCP/UDP/SCTP checksum (firewall vs end-host fingerprint).
.TP
.B \-D \fIDECOY1,DECOY2,...,ME,...\fR
Decoy cloaking.
.B ME
inserts your real source at that position.
.TP
.B \-S \fIIP\fR
Spoof source IP. Combine with
.B \-e iface
when needed.
.TP
.B \-\-data \fIHEX\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-data-string \fITEXT\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-data-length \fIN\fR
Append payload to packets.
.B \-\-data-length
alone appends
.I N
zero bytes.
.TP
.B \-f
Use small fragments (8-byte payload chunks). Parsed only; no fragmentation
is performed.
.TP
.B \-\-mtu \fIVAL\fR
Custom fragmentation MTU (must be a multiple of 8). Parsed only.
.TP
.B \-\-spoof-mac \fIMAC\fR
Spoof source MAC on ARP discovery frames (full MAC, prefix, or vendor
name).
.TP
.B \-e \fIIFACE\fR
Force use of a specific interface. Parsed only; ARP discovery still picks the
first up, non-loopback IPv4 interface.
.SH "10. PROXY"
.TP
.B \-\-proxies \fIURLS\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-proxy \fIURLS\fR
Comma-separated proxy URLs for TCP-connect scans. Supports
.B socks4://
and
.B http://
(HTTP CONNECT). Example:
.B socks4://127.0.0.1:1080,http://10.0.0.1:8080
.SH "11. OUTPUT"
.TP
.BR \-oN " " \fIFILE\fR
Normal (human-readable) output.
.TP
.BR \-oG " " \fIFILE\fR
Grepable output (one host per line).
.TP
.BR \-oX " " \fIFILE\fR
XML output. Root
.B <nmaprun>
with
.BR <scaninfo> ,
.BR <host> ,
.BR <status> ,
.BR <address> ,
.BR <hostnames> ,
.BR <ports> ,
.BR <extraports> ,
.BR <service> ,
.BR <runstats >
\(em nmap-compatible.
.TP
.BR \-oA " " \fIBASE\fR
Write
.IR BASE .{nmap,gnmap,xml}
in one go.
.TP
.BR \-oS " " \fIFILE\fR
Script-kiddie output (1337-speak mirror of
.BR \-oN ;
stdout stays normal).
.TP
.BR \-oM " " \fIFILE\fR
Machine-readable (currently same lines as
.BR \-oG ).
.TP
.BR \-oH " " \fIFILE\fR
Placeholder hex output (full hex capture not implemented).
.TP
.B \-\-stylesheet \fIURL\fR
.TQ
.B \-\-webxml
.TQ
.B \-\-no-stylesheet
XML preamble /
.B xml-stylesheet
PI control when
.B \-oX
is used.
.TP
.B \-\-append-output
Append to output files instead of clobber.
.SH "12. MISC"
.TP
.B \-6
IPv6 targets and scans (including raw SYN when privileged).
.TP
.B \-A
Aggressive:
.B \-O
+
.B \-sV
+
.B \-sC
+
.BR \-\-traceroute .
Not full nmap NSE/Lua.
.TP
.B \-\-resume \fIFILE\fR
Resume from JSON checkpoint of completed
.BR "(host, port)" .
The checkpoint is subtracted from the work list before scan dispatch, so it
applies to every port-scan kind: TCP connect, UDP, raw half-open TCP, SCTP,
IP protocol, idle and FTP bounce (remaining pairs only).
.TP
.B \-\-iflist
List interfaces via
.BR if-addrs .
.TP
.B \-\-privileged
Force raw mode (kernel may still reject without root /
.BR CAP_NET_RAW ).
.TP
.B \-\-unprivileged
Force TCP connect mode even as root; rejects raw-only modes
.RB ( \-sO ,
.BR \-sI ,
SCTP).
.TP
.B \-\-allports
Ignore
.B \-\-exclude-ports
when set.
.TP
.B \-\-datadir \fIPATH\fR
Override the default
.B ./data
directory for nmap reference files
.RB ( nmap-services ,
.BR nmap-service-probes ,
.BR nmap-os-db ,
.BR nmap-protocols ).
Also honors the
.B NMAPDIR
env var.
.TP
.B \-\-versiondb \fIPATH\fR
Specific version probe database file.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-vv
Increase verbosity.
.TP
.B \-d
Increase debug level. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.B \-V\fR, \-\-version
Print version.
.SH "13. PARITY MATRIX"
Status vs upstream
.BR nmap (1).
See README for the full table; abridged below.
.PP
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
.B Area|.B Status
TCP connect (-sT)|Implemented
TCP SYN raw (-sS, IPv4 + IPv6)|Implemented (privileged)
TCP NULL/FIN/Xmas/Maimon|Implemented (raw, sharded pipeline)
TCP ACK / Window (-sA / -sW)|Implemented (no connect fallback)
UDP (-sU)|Implemented (raw ICMP listener for unreach)
SCTP INIT / COOKIE-ECHO (-sY / -sZ)|Implemented (IPv4 + IPv6, CRC32c)
Idle scan (-sI)|Implemented (IPv4 only, sequential IP-ID)
FTP bounce (-b)|Implemented (IPv4 only)
IP protocol (-sO)|Implemented (IPv4 + IPv6 on Unix)
Ping scan (-sn)|Implemented
Host discovery (-PS/-PA/-PU/-PY/-PO/-PE/-PP/-PM)|Implemented
ARP ping (no flag, local IPv4)|Implemented (auto)
IPv6 (-6)|Implemented
-iL / -iR|Implemented
--resume|Implemented (every port-scan kind)
--traceroute|Implemented (system traceroute, concurrent)
-O OS detection|Partial (IPv4 raw + DB scoring; IPv6 TTL heuristic)
-A aggressive bundle|Implemented (no NSE/Lua)
-sV service/version|Partial (no Perl-only regex; rest implemented)
--script / -sC|Partial (default + banner builtins; no Lua NSE)
--iflist|Implemented
--host-timeout|Implemented
--max-retries|Implemented (omits scan-delay / rate pacer on retry)
--min-rtt / --max-rtt / --initial-rtt timeout|Implemented
--scan-delay / --max-scan-delay|Implemented
--max-rate / --min-rate|Implemented (one global limiter)
--min-hostgroup / --max-hostgroup|Implemented
--scanflags|Implemented (raw TCP scans only)
Port specs (-p, -F, --top-ports, --port-ratio)|Implemented
Evasion (-g, --badsum, -D, -S, --data*, --spoof-mac)|Implemented (packet-level)
--ttl, -f / --mtu, --ip-options, -e, --send-eth/--send-ip|Parsed only (not applied)
--proxies / --proxy|Implemented (SOCKS4 + HTTP CONNECT)
--dns-servers|Implemented (hickory-resolver)
Auto privilege detection|Implemented
-oN, -oG, -oX, -oA, -oS|Implemented (nmap-compatible XML)
-oM|Partial (same as -oG)
-oH|Partial (placeholder)
--stylesheet / --webxml / --no-stylesheet|Partial
--resolve-all|Implemented
--unprivileged / --privileged|Implemented
--allports|Implemented
--osscan-limit / --osscan-guess / --max-os-tries|Partial
--script-timeout|Partial
--stats-every|Implemented
NSE Lua runtime|Not implemented
.TE
.PP
If you need authoritative nmap NSE/OS-DB behavior, use
.BR nmap (1).
.SH "14. ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Suppress ANSI color in terminal output.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter (see
.BR tracing-subscriber 's
EnvFilter).
.SH "15. FILES"
.TP
.I ./data/nmap-service-probes
Service / version probe definitions, read by
.BR \-sV .
Not committed; fetch with
.IR scripts/fetch_nmap_data.sh .
Override the path with
.BR \-\-versiondb .
.TP
.I ./data/nmap-os-db
OS fingerprint database, read by
.BR \-O .
Not committed; fetch with
.IR scripts/fetch_nmap_data.sh .
.TP
.I ./data/top_ports.txt
TCP port frequency list, compiled into the binary.
.TP
.I ./data/nmap_ip_protocols_fast.txt
Fast-mode protocol shortlist for
.BR "\-sO \-F" ,
compiled into the binary.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/nmaprs.1
Short reference man page.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/nmaprsall.1
This man page.
.SH "16. EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Scan completed (regardless of host/port states).
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error: missing privileges, no target resolved, no host responded to
discovery, or an I/O error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid CLI usage (unknown flag, missing or malformed argument value).
.SH "17. EXAMPLES"
.PP
Basic TCP connect of common ports:
.RS
.nf
nmaprs scanme.nmap.org
.fi
.RE
.PP
Quick top-100 port SYN scan against a /24 (privileged):
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-sS \-F 192.168.1.0/24
.fi
.RE
.PP
Full TCP port range (1\-65535) with version + OS detection:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-sS \-p \- \-sV \-O scanme.nmap.org
.fi
.RE
.PP
Aggressive scan, all three output formats:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-A \-T4 target \-oA scan-results
.fi
.RE
.PP
UDP scan of top 100 ports through a SOCKS4 proxy:
.RS
.nf
nmaprs \-sU \-\-top-ports 100 \-\-proxies socks4://127.0.0.1:1080 target
.fi
.RE
.PP
Idle scan via a zombie host:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-sI zombie.example.com:65535 target
.fi
.RE
.PP
FTP bounce:
.RS
.nf
nmaprs \-b anonymous@ftp.example.com 10.0.0.0/24
.fi
.RE
.PP
SCTP INIT scan:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-sY \-p 80,443 sctp-host
.fi
.RE
.PP
IP-protocol scan of all 256 protocols (Unix, privileged):
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-sO target
.fi
.RE
.PP
Custom DNS resolvers + custom user-agent style payload:
.RS
.nf
nmaprs \-\-dns-servers 1.1.1.1,8.8.8.8 \-\-data-length 64 target
.fi
.RE
.PP
NULL scan with custom TCP flags + spoofed source port:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-sN \-\-scanflags "FIN URG PSH" \-g 53 target
.fi
.RE
.PP
Decoy cloaking + spoofed source IP:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-sS \-D RND:5,ME \-S 192.0.2.1 target
.fi
.RE
.PP
Host discovery on a local subnet (ARP ping runs automatically for
local-subnet IPv4 hosts):
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-sn 192.168.1.0/24
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read targets from file, exclude one subnet, write grepable output:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-\-iL targets.txt \-\-exclude 10.0.0.0/16 \-oG out.gnmap
.fi
.RE
.PP
IPv6 SYN scan with all-ports timing template T4:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-6 \-sS \-p \- \-T4 2001:db8::1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Resume an interrupted scan:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-\-resume nmaprs.checkpoint.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Periodic progress + per-host timeout cap:
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-sS \-\-stats-every 30s \-\-host-timeout 5m target
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rate-limited polite scan (T1 + min/max-rate):
.RS
.nf
sudo nmaprs \-sS \-T1 \-\-min-rate 10 \-\-max-rate 100 target
.fi
.RE
.PP
List interfaces:
.RS
.nf
nmaprs \-\-iflist
.fi
.RE
.SH "18. SECURITY / ETHICS"
Run only against networks and hosts you own or have explicit written
permission to scan. Unauthorized scanning is illegal in many
jurisdictions. The author and contributors disclaim responsibility
for misuse.
